&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Day 243 fairy lights</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/day-243-fairy-lights/</link><pubDate>Mon, 25 Nov 2013 20:25:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/day-243-fairy-lights/</guid><description>&lt;div xmlns='http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml'&gt;&lt;img style='max-width:586px;' src='http://farm6.staticflickr.com/5507/11054984516_fe109f27a4_b.jpg'/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;div&gt;http://flic.kr/p/hQTFKj, December 08, 2002 at 12:00PM&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Day 240 Breakroom view</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/day-240-breakroom-view/</link><pubDate>Fri, 22 Nov 2013 16:13:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/day-240-breakroom-view/</guid><description>&lt;div xmlns='http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml'&gt;&lt;img style='max-width:586px;' src='http://farm4.staticflickr.com/3790/10995652985_006e027fa1_b.jpg'/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;div&gt;http://flic.kr/p/hKDAxT, November 22, 2013 at 02:50PM&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Nexus 5 One Week On</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/nexus-5-one-week-on/</link><pubDate>Wed, 13 Nov 2013 09:59:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/nexus-5-one-week-on/</guid><description>&lt;div dir="ltr" style="text-align: left;" trbidi="on"&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="http://www.flickr.com/photos/doodle_m/10677122173/" title="Day 222 Nexus 5 by Alastair Montgomery, on Flickr"&gt;&lt;img alt="Day 222 Nexus 5" src="http://farm4.staticflickr.com/3682/10677122173_a87c6efa36_c.jpg" height="800" width="600" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;div dir="ltr" style="text-align: left;" trbidi="on"&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;After my first week with my 32gb Nexus 5 here are some initial thoughts compared to my previous phone Samsung Galaxy S2. Nothing major to complain about.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;u&gt;Likes&lt;/u&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;ul style="text-align: left;"&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Camera App and its better integration with Google Plus and on phone picture editing.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;The screen is very good.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Feels very fast, good response in switching apps, swiping between screens and scrolling.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;u&gt;Dislikes&lt;/u&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;ul style="text-align: left;"&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;You can assign custom ringtones from Google Play Music, had to resort to a third party app to get ringtones assigned.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Alarm has some functionality removed like the smart alarm "soft" wake up.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="http://meekgonkey.blogspot.com/"&gt;Doodle's Geek Monkey&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="http://twitter.com/alastair_hm"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Day 224 Office Highlights</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/day-224-office-highlights/</link><pubDate>Wed, 06 Nov 2013 12:55:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/day-224-office-highlights/</guid><description>&lt;div xmlns='http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml'&gt;&lt;img style='max-width:586px;' src='http://farm4.staticflickr.com/3729/10707111536_a1b66d6e1f_b.jpg'/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;div&gt;No one is that happy in the office? http://flic.kr/p/hj9Kej, November 06, 2013 at 12:20PM&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>